#!markdown

# mr-load run sheet — the sequence, nothing else

The compass notebook (`mr-load-compass.dib`) is for setting a machine up once: routes, `.env`
clinic, Google login. This one assumes that is done and answers three questions every time you
sit down: **where am I, what is next, run it.** Sixteen steps, one cell each, in the only order
that is valid. Every step is idempotent (`scripts/run_pass1.sh`), records a checkpoint in
`.mrload/checkpoints.tsv`, and the state cell reads those checkpoints back.

| # | step | gate | what must be true afterwards |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `preflight` | | tools, `.env`, Drive root visible, token → sandbox portal, BigQuery reachable |
| 2 | `walk` | | `.mrload/library_hierarchy.csv` written, node count plausible, no ERROR |
| 3 | `bq-init` | | datasets + empty ledger tables exist |
| 4 | `bq-load` | LIVE `BQ_LOAD` | `mrload_raw.library_hierarchy` replaced with the CSV |
| 5 | `hs-props` | LIVE `PROPERTY_CREATE` | property definitions exist in the portal (`exists`/`created`, no `type_mismatch`) |
| 6 | `dbt` | | **0 FAIL** — the cardinality gate; WARN on orphans is allowed |
| 7 | `hs-props-verify` | | every mapping row `ok` → `.mrload/review/stacksync_mapping.csv` (StackSync UI) |
| 8 | `review` | | queues written; `multi_parent.csv` empty; `deal_decisions.csv` ready to edit |
| 9 | `companies-dry` | | `ambiguous_match = 0` |
| 10 | `companies-live` | LIVE `COMPANY_CREATE` | ledger `companies_resolved` populated |
| 11 | `attach-dry` | | row count = files under resolved companies |
| 12 | `attach-upload` | LIVE `FILES_UPLOAD` | ledger `files_uploaded` all `uploaded` |
| 13 | `attach-notes` | LIVE `FILE_NOTES_POST` | ledger `file_notes_posted` all `attached` |
| 14 | `ledger-export` | LIVE `BQ_LOAD` | HubSpot ids visible in silver; StackSync syncs can be enabled |
| 15 | `deals-dry` | | pass 2, only after `approve=Y` rows exist in `deal_decisions.csv` |
| 16 | `deals-live` | LIVE `DEAL_CREATE` | then `ledger-export` once more (deal ids back to BigQuery) |

**Rules the sequence enforces**
- A step counts as done only if its last successful run is newer than every step before it. Re-running `walk` makes 3–14 pending again. That is intended.
- A LIVE step first re-runs its dry counterpart, then fires. In this notebook a LIVE cell is refused until `$ConfirmLive = $true`; with it set, `YES_ALL=1` answers the runner's prompts, so the flag is your confirmation.
- Anything that stops the run (dbt FAIL, ambiguous company names, `type_mismatch`, a 403) is recorded as `failed` and stays the next step until it passes.

#!mermaid

flowchart LR
    s1["1 preflight"] --> s2["2 walk"] --> s3["3 bq-init"] --> s4["4 bq-load ⟨LIVE⟩"] --> s5["5 hs-props ⟨LIVE⟩"] --> s6{"6 dbt\n0 FAIL ?"}
    s6 -- no --> stop((stop))
    s6 -- yes --> s7["7 hs-props-verify"] --> s8["8 review"] --> s9["9 companies-dry"] --> s10["10 companies-live ⟨LIVE⟩"]
    s10 --> s11["11 attach-dry"] --> s12["12 attach-upload ⟨LIVE⟩"] --> s13["13 attach-notes ⟨LIVE⟩"] --> s14["14 ledger-export ⟨LIVE⟩"]
    s14 -. "approve=Y rows" .-> s15["15 deals-dry"] --> s16["16 deals-live ⟨LIVE⟩"] --> s14b["ledger-export again"]

#!markdown

## 0 · Switches + helpers — run first, every time

Same switches as the compass. The helper functions live in `notebooks/mr-load-helpers.ps1`
(shared by both notebooks); this cell finds and loads them. `$ConfirmLive` stays `$false` until
you have read a dry output and mean it.

#!pwsh

# ── switches ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
$Route       = 'wsl'                                   # 'wsl' | 'devcontainer' | 'linux'
$Distro      = 'Ubuntu-24.04'
$RepoWsl     = '~/mir-load'                            # route wsl: clone on the Linux side
$RepoWin     = "$HOME\mir-load"                        # route devcontainer: Windows clone (also where this notebook is looked up)
$Image       = 'mrload-ubuntu'
$RepoLinux   = '/workspaces/mir-load'                  # route linux: notebook opened inside Ubuntu / the Dev Container
$ConfirmLive = $false                                  # $true = LIVE steps fire (BigQuery + HubSpot writes), prompts answered

# ── load notebooks/mr-load-helpers.ps1 ──────────────────────────────────────
$candidates = @((Join-Path $RepoWin 'notebooks\mr-load-helpers.ps1'),
                (Join-Path $PWD 'mr-load-helpers.ps1'),
                (Join-Path $PWD 'notebooks\mr-load-helpers.ps1'),
                (Join-Path $RepoLinux 'notebooks/mr-load-helpers.ps1'))
if ($Route -eq 'wsl' -and (Get-Command wsl.exe -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)) {
    $env:WSL_UTF8 = '1'
    $linuxHome  = (wsl.exe -d $Distro -e bash -lc 'echo $HOME' | Select-Object -First 1).Trim()
    $candidates += "\\wsl$\$Distro" + ((($RepoWsl -replace '^~', $linuxHome) -replace '/', '\')) + '\notebooks\mr-load-helpers.ps1'
}
$helpers = $candidates | Where-Object { $_ -and (Test-Path $_) } | Select-Object -First 1
if (-not $helpers) { throw "mr-load-helpers.ps1 not found. Looked in: $($candidates -join ' | '). Set `$RepoWin to your Windows clone (or open the repo folder in VS Code) and re-run." }
Invoke-Expression (Get-Content -Raw $helpers)
"helpers: $helpers"
Show-Route

#!markdown

## 1 · Where am I?

Reads `.mrload/checkpoints.tsv` and the artefacts. `done` / `stale` / `failed` / `pending` per
step, evidence (row counts, ledger statuses, dbt test summary), and the **next** step in order.
Run it whenever you come back; run it after any failure.

#!pwsh

Get-PipelineState

#!markdown

## 2 · The sequence — one cell per step, top to bottom

Each cell is `Invoke-Step '<name>'`, which is `scripts/run_pass1.sh <name>` inside Ubuntu. LIVE
cells carry the gate inline and are refused until `$ConfirmLive = $true`. Re-running a cell is
always safe: every step skips what is already done and converges.

