#!markdown

## 3 · Streamlined patterns

**Next only.** One cell, run it again and again: it looks up the next pending step (stale
predecessors first) and runs exactly that one.

#!pwsh

Invoke-NextStep

#!markdown

**Everything dry, then decide.** Runs every pending step in order and stops in front of the first
LIVE gate, whatever `$ConfirmLive` says. Read the dry output, then either `Invoke-Step` the LIVE
step or run this cell again with `$ConfirmLive = $true` set in the Switches cell.

#!pwsh

Invoke-Sequence -UntilLive

#!markdown

**Through a target.** With `$ConfirmLive = $true` this fires every gate on the way, in order,
without prompts, and halts at the first failure. Typical: `-Through 'ledger-export'` for the whole
of pass 1 after a clean `Invoke-Sequence -UntilLive`.

#!pwsh

Invoke-Sequence -Through 'ledger-export'

#!markdown

## 4 · Status and stop rules

| the state cell says | it means | you do |
|---|---|---|
| `failed` on `dbt` | a cardinality test failed (multi-parent file, duplicate company name in a segment, tradeshow leak) | fix in Drive → `walk` → the sequence re-enters at `bq-load` |
| `failed` on `companies-live` | ambiguous names | merge or rename in HubSpot → `companies-dry` |
| `failed` on `hs-props` | `type_mismatch` or 403 | fix the card or the private-app scopes → `hs-props` |
| `stale` on 3–14 | `walk` ran again | just continue, the order is preserved |
| `partial` in the attach ledger | note created, association failed | re-run `attach-notes`, it converges |

#!pwsh

Invoke-Step 'status'
Invoke-Ubuntu 'scripts/dev/last_log.sh 30'

#!markdown

## 5 · Rollback — LIVE `MRLOAD_APPROVE_UNMIGRATE`
Deletes every note this pipeline attached (ledger is the index). Files, companies and deals stay.

#!pwsh

Invoke-Step 'unmigrate'
